node_modules/

# TypeScript build artifacts.
schema/dist/
renderer/dist/
cli/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Build output: tsup bundles cli/ into bin/, and bin/ is what npm publishes.
# Not committed — unlike the rendered trees at the repo root (claude/, cursor/,
# ohmypi/, opencode/), which are meant to be diffed in review. A bundle diff is
# noise, and `i:build` regenerates it before every publish.
bin/

# Working notes and session handoffs — personal state, not the team's.
#
# vwf's memory doctrine splits its seven rooms: `decisions`, `planning`, `gaps`
# and `problems` are the team's and stay committed; `handoff`, `doctor` and
# `runs` are one developer's state and are not. Only `docs/scratchpad/` was ever
# listed here, so the comment described a rule half of which did not exist and
# every `/vwf:handoff` committed a personal handoff. `doctor/` and `runs/` are
# listed before they exist on purpose — they are written by a command, so the
# first run that creates one would otherwise reintroduce exactly this bug.
docs/scratchpad/
docs/memory/handoff/
docs/memory/doctor/
docs/memory/runs/

# This repo's own Cursor plugin install, which is a developer's choice rather
# than the project's. Cursor has no user scope — marketplace installs there are
# account-side — so `--platform cursor` always lands in the working project, and
# here that working project is this repo. Committing it would also pin every
# reader to `main` via `gitUrl`, since a Cursor source takes no ref.
#
# Not to be confused with `cursor/`, the committed render tree, or
# `.cursor-plugin/`, the generated marketplace manifest at the repo root.
.cursor/
